13 Hours: The Secret Soldiers of Benghazi is a 2016 American biographical
action-thriller film, directed and produced by Michael Bay.

12
01:18:32,727 --> 01:18:38,727
Written by Chuck Hogan, it is based on the 2014 non-fiction book
13 Hours by American author Mitchell Zuckoff.

13
01:25:05,454 --> 01:25:11,454
The film follows six members of the Annex Security Team who fought to defend the American diplomatic
compound in Benghazi, Libya after waves of attacks by militants on September 11, 2012.

14
01:31:38,181 --> 01:31:44,181
The film stars James Badge Dale, John Krasinski, Pablo Schreiber, Max Martini, David Denman and
Dominic Fumusa, with supporting roles by Toby Stephens, Alexia Barlier and David Costabile.

15
01:38:10,909 --> 01:38:16,909
Filming on location began on April 27, 2015, in Libya.

16
01:44:43,636 --> 01:44:49,636
Upon its release on January 15, 2016, by Paramount Pictures, 13 Hours grossed over $69 million worldwide
against a production budget of $50 million, becoming one of Bay's lowest-grossing films.

17
